Hence \(A_m\) will \(= 0\), and consequently the \(m\)th tone of the string will disappear when \(\sin\frac{m\pi a}{l} = 0\), that is, when \(a = \frac{l}{m}\) or \(= \frac{2l}{m}\), or \(= \frac{3l}{m}\), &c. Hence we suppose the string to be divided into \(m\) equal parts, and@@A@@
>>>
<<<
@@A@@
===
 to be plucked in one of these divisions, the \(m\)th tone disappears, and this is the tone whose nodes fall upon these points.

Every node for an \(m\)th tone is also a node for the \(2m\)th, \(3m\)th, \(4m\)th, &c., tone, and hence all these tones also disappear.
@@A@@
>>>
